  "body": "Hello David,\n\nThank you for your feedback.\n\nAt this stage, the pricing is still not at the level required for successful \nentry into the key retail channels. From our perspective, we would need to \ntarget approximately a 40% discount to ensure competitiveness.\n\nAchieving this level would enable us to proceed with launches in Watsons, \nRossmann, and Gratis, which together represent a network of over 1,500 doors \nand a significant growth opportunity for the brand in Turkey.\n\nPlease let us know your thoughts on whether this could be workable.\n\nBest regards,\nOkan Can\n\nOn Wed, Apr 22, 2026 at 8:53 AM David I Daejin Park 박대진 <david@yogico.kr \n<mailto:david@yogico.kr> > wrote:\n\nHi Orkan,\n\nWe made a strong case for your company during our discussions with Vussen \nand were able to achieve a meaningful price improvement.\n\nSpecifically for toothpaste, we secured pricing at approximately 27–30% \nbelow the original quotation:\n\n*\tOrders below 100,000 pcs: USD 2.40 (approx. 27% discount)\n*\tOrders of 100,000 pcs or more: USD 2.30 (approx. 30% discount)\n\nKindly note that the this FOB pricing may be subject to minor adjustments \ndepending on exchange rate fluctuations, as it is calculated based on KRW.\n\nFor your reference, the Nordic buyer has recently placed the first order of \n200,000 units. The lead time is about 6-8 weeks.\n\nBest Regards,\n\nDavid I Daejin Park  박대진, CEO\nYogi Corporation Inc.\n\nAddress: 201, 125, Bongeunsa-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, Korea\nMobile: +82 10 6747 9443\n <http://www.yogico.kr/> www.yogico.kr",
  "truncated": false
 },
 {
  "id": "6aa0d3a38f83165dc75cea3f",
  "subject": "Request for Low-Cost K-Beauty Brands for Portfolio Expansion",
  "from": "Andreea Ciucu <andreea.ciucu@my-k.ro>",
  "to": "david@yogico.kr",
  "date": "2026-04-21",
  "folder": "INBOX.My K Romania",
  "group": "My K Romania",
  "hasAttach": 1,
  "ruleClass": "unknown",
  "lead": "My K Retail & Distribution (Romania)",
  "body": "Dear David,\n\nI hope you are doing well.\n\nI am reaching out to discuss a new strategic direction we are currently \ndeveloping on our side.\n\nDue to the current economic context in Romania, consumer behavior has \nshifted significantly. We are experiencing a decrease in overall \nconsumption, with customers becoming much more price-sensitive and \nincreasingly oriented towards affordable products.\n\nAs a result, we are now focusing on expanding our portfolio with entry-level \nK-beauty brands that can offer strong retail competitiveness, ideally with a \nminimum x5 markup coefficient.\n\nTo give you a clearer idea of our target positioning, we are currently \nlooking for products within the following price ranges:\n\n*\tSheet masks: USD 0.10 – 0.14 / pc\n*\tFace creams: around USD 2.50\n*\tSerums: around USD 3.00\n\nWe already have one brand in our portfolio that meets these criteria, and it \nis performing very successfully across Romania. Moreover, we have recently \nreceived strong interest from an international retailer in Ukraine (with \nover 1,800 stores) for this type of product segment.\n\nIn this context, we would highly appreciate your support in identifying at \nleast 1–2 suitable brands from your portfolio (or network) that could match \nthis positioning in terms of:\n\n*\tpricing\n*\tproduct quality\n*\tscalability for large retail distribution\n\nIt is also very important for us that the products already have CPNP \nregistration (or can obtain it quickly), in order to ensure a fast and \ncompliant launch on the European market.\n\nWe believe this segment will become increasingly important in the coming \nperiod, and we are keen to move quickly in securing the right partnerships.\n\nThank you in advance for your support, and we look forward to your \nsuggestions.\n\nKind regards,",
  "truncated": false
 },
